WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:31.708
In the second verse of Chapter 16,

2
00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:32.625
Lord Krishna now

3
00:00:32.625 --> 00:00:35.625
continues the list of divine qualities.

4
00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:36.500
He is here

5
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.958
specifically describing the qualities

6
00:00:38.958 --> 00:00:42.375
that bring peace to relationships

7
00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.541
and bring the inner emotions into balance.

8
00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:46.708
These are the very qualities

9
00:00:46.708 --> 00:00:49.625
that lead the seeker toward liberation

10
00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:52.791
and make them a well-wisher of all.

11
00:00:57.625 --> 00:00:59.041
One by one

12
00:00:59.041 --> 00:01:00.750
He gives the features of several

13
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.916
more important qualities.

14
00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:06.875
First, ahimsa – non-violence.

15
00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:10.125
This is not merely avoiding physical harm.

16
00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:11.416
It means

17
00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:15.000
not obstructing anyone's growth, whether

18
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.041
it is physical, mental, or spiritual.

19
00:01:19.041 --> 00:01:20.000
True non-violence

20
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.958
brings compassion into speech,
thought, and intention.

21
00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:27.666
It arises from deep empathy

22
00:01:27.666 --> 00:01:31.750
and keeps one away from
exploitation and humiliation.

23
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.333
Satyam – truthfulness.

24
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.875
Truth is not only stating facts.

25
00:01:36.875 --> 00:01:38.250
It is speech

26
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.250
that is beneficial, appropriate, and
conducive to growth.

27
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.666
It also includes being honest with oneself

28
00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:49.166
and avoiding distortion for personal gain.

29
00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:54.000
Akrodhah – absence of anger.

30
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.791
Anger is born

31
00:01:55.791 --> 00:01:58.625
when desires are not fulfilled.

32
00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:03.000
Akrodha means tolerance and forgiveness –

33
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.166
especially when provoked.

34
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:08.041
This is not suppressing anger,

35
00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:11.166
but responding with wisdom.

36
00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:13.666
Such a person is strong within

37
00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:17.791
and sees with far-reaching perspective.

38
00:02:17.791 --> 00:02:21.625
Tyagah – renunciation.

39
00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:24.583
This is not abandoning responsibility.

40
00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:26.000
It means

41
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.500
giving up the craving for ownership and control.

42
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.750
True renunciation

43
00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.166
is acting without expectation of results.

44
00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:36.541
It is also the capacity

45
00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:40.791
to let go of ego, bitterness, and expectations.

46
00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:45.166
Shantih – peace.

47
00:02:45.166 --> 00:02:48.416
Peace means steadiness of mind,

48
00:02:48.416 --> 00:02:51.666
even when there is a storm outside.

49
00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:52.541
This peace

50
00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:55.958
is born from a deep sense of surrender.

51
00:02:55.958 --> 00:02:59.208
Such a person is neither easily agitated,

52
00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:01.666
nor does he unsettle others.

53
00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:06.208
Their very presence brings others comfort.

54
00:03:06.208 --> 00:03:10.875
Apaishunam – absence of slander.

55
00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:14.666
Paishunam means gossip and
speaking ill of others,

56
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:17.875
especially in their absence.

57
00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:20.166
Apaishunam is its opposite –

58
00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.458
not counting others'

59
00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:25.000
faults and bringing out their virtues.

60
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.083
This is the mark of a humble and pure mind.

61
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:32.916
Daya bhuteshu means

62
00:03:32.916 --> 00:03:35.875
compassion toward all beings.

63
00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:38.208
This is an extension of non-violence.

64
00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:40.125
Daya is active compassion –

65
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:44.000
the readiness to reduce others' suffering.

66
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.625
And bhuteshu means all beings;

67
00:03:47.625 --> 00:03:49.375
not only humans.

68
00:03:49.375 --> 00:03:55.041
Such a person sees every life as sacred
and worthy of respect.

69
00:03:55.041 --> 00:03:56.416
Aloluptvam

70
00:03:56.416 --> 00:03:59.375
means absence of greed.

71
00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:02.833
Greed means insatiability.

72
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:06.000
Aloluptvam means the absence of greed.

73
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.000
Contentment

74
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.291
with what has been received,
and the readiness to share it.

75
00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:16.458
This teaches generosity, not accumulation.

76
00:04:16.458 --> 00:04:19.958
Mardavam – gentleness.

77
00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:22.333
This is softness in behaviour.

78
00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:26.458
No bitterness, no harshness, no pride.

79
00:04:26.458 --> 00:04:27.250
Such a person

80
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.750
understands others' feelings,

81
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.458
speaks with humility,

82
00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:34.541
and does not become aggressive in response.

83
00:04:34.541 --> 00:04:38.458
This is the gentle form of strength.

84
00:04:38.458 --> 00:04:42.666
Hrih – modesty.

85
00:04:42.666 --> 00:04:44.750
Hrih is the natural hesitation

86
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.375
that keeps one away from improper conduct.

87
00:04:47.375 --> 00:04:51.833
It is inner conscience that
protects from hypocrisy

88
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:55.083
and keeps a person humble.

89
00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:57.291
Achapalam means

90
00:04:57.291 --> 00:05:00.833
steadiness, free from impatience.

91
00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:05.375
Chapalata means instability and impatience.

92
00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:07.416
Achapalam means

93
00:05:07.416 --> 00:05:11.041
remaining steady in resolve and conduct.

94
00:05:11.041 --> 00:05:14.583
It prevents attention and action from scattering

95
00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:17.416
and keeps the seeker centred.

96
00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:24.000
Compassion is not limited to

97
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.000
occasionally helping someone.

98
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.666
Daya bhuteshu means

99
00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:35.916
compassion toward all beings,

100
00:05:35.916 --> 00:05:38.625
not only toward those you love.

101
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:42.083
Not only toward humans, but toward every

102
00:05:42.083 --> 00:05:45.125
soul that breathes,

103
00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:48.500
walks, crawls, or flies.

104
00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.833
You do not need to do something great.

105
00:05:52.833 --> 00:05:54.000
Sometimes

106
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.750
simply pausing before reacting,

107
00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:02.916
or thinking before speaking, is also compassion.

108
00:06:02.916 --> 00:06:06.458
Being gentle when a child makes a mistake,

109
00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:10.000
or not trampling a small creature

110
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:14.208
that comes across your path –
this too is compassion.

111
00:06:14.208 --> 00:06:17.375
When you see others as separate from you,

112
00:06:17.375 --> 00:06:19.583
distance is created.

113
00:06:19.583 --> 00:06:22.875
But when you begin to see every life

114
00:06:22.875 --> 00:06:26.166
as connected to Me,

115
00:06:26.166 --> 00:06:29.000
the heart becomes tender.

116
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.291
Then you no longer ask –

117
00:06:31.291 --> 00:06:34.125
‘Are they worthy of compassion?’

118
00:06:34.125 --> 00:06:37.291
You begin to ask –

119
00:06:37.291 --> 00:06:38.708
‘Can I

120
00:06:38.708 --> 00:06:42.208
express my love in this moment?’

121
00:06:42.208 --> 00:06:47.541
You cannot solve every problem, but

122
00:06:47.541 --> 00:06:52.541
you can choose to be compassionate,
again and again.

123
00:06:52.541 --> 00:06:54.291
This choice, made again and again,

124
00:06:54.291 --> 00:06:59.500
is what truly makes the soul divine.

125
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.833
In close relationships,

126
00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:09.958
it is very easy to see each other's shortcomings.

127
00:07:09.958 --> 00:07:13.291
Living under the same roof, small things

128
00:07:13.291 --> 00:07:16.541
catch attention – habits, words,

129
00:07:16.541 --> 00:07:19.875
even the tone of speaking.

130
00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:23.416
But apaishunam,

131
00:07:23.416 --> 00:07:28.375
refraining from fault-finding, is a divine quality.

132
00:07:28.375 --> 00:07:30.541
Not constantly pointing out

133
00:07:30.541 --> 00:07:33.958
every mistake is not weakness.

134
00:07:33.958 --> 00:07:35.500
It is wisdom.

135
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:39.041
When you focus only on faults,

136
00:07:39.041 --> 00:07:43.458
the doors of your heart begin to close.

137
00:07:43.458 --> 00:07:46.375
You stop seeing the person

138
00:07:46.375 --> 00:07:50.916
and start seeing only the problem.

139
00:07:50.916 --> 00:07:54.791
Slowly, distance grows. But

140
00:07:54.791 --> 00:07:58.500
when you bring out the good qualities,

141
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:02.625
even small things create closeness

142
00:08:02.625 --> 00:08:05.916
and room for growth.

143
00:08:05.916 --> 00:08:07.250
Your family does not

144
00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.500
always need a critic.

145
00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:15.875
They need a compassionate witness.

146
00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:19.375
Be the one who sees the effort,

147
00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:21.916
not only the error.

148
00:08:21.916 --> 00:08:24.583
Be not only the one who corrects,

149
00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:27.416
but also the one who lifts.

150
00:08:27.416 --> 00:08:29.250
This does not mean

151
00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.666
that necessary improvements
should be ignored.

152
00:08:32.666 --> 00:08:35.833
But say them with love.

153
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:40.208
Choose your words carefully.

154
00:08:40.208 --> 00:08:43.958
When you stop looking for faults

155
00:08:43.958 --> 00:08:47.708
and start looking for the good in others,

156
00:08:47.708 --> 00:08:52.208
your home becomes a divine place of shelter.

157
00:08:56.916 --> 00:09:00.666
At the workplace there is always pressure.

158
00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:03.541
More of everything is wanted –

159
00:09:03.541 --> 00:09:07.208
recognition, reward, speed.

160
00:09:07.208 --> 00:09:09.583
And remember –

161
00:09:09.583 --> 00:09:12.041
aloluptvam.

162
00:09:12.041 --> 00:09:14.291
Freedom from greed,

163
00:09:14.291 --> 00:09:18.708
and achapalam – steadiness free

164
00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:22.416
from restlessness – both are divine qualities.

165
00:09:22.416 --> 00:09:27.000
Greed is not only chasing money.

166
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.833
It also shows up in comparison,

167
00:09:29.833 --> 00:09:31.500
in impatience,

168
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.458
and in the habit of never being satisfied.

169
00:09:35.458 --> 00:09:38.750
And restlessness shows

170
00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:42.208
when you keep changing tasks again and again,

171
00:09:42.208 --> 00:09:47.333
but are never truly present in any one of them.

172
00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:50.916
But when you find contentment

173
00:09:50.916 --> 00:09:55.125
in what you have, and in the work you are in,

174
00:09:55.125 --> 00:09:57.958
you remain focused,

175
00:09:57.958 --> 00:10:00.583
then everything changes.

176
00:10:00.583 --> 00:10:05.666
You stop running, you stop chasing,

177
00:10:05.666 --> 00:10:09.791
and you actually begin to move forward.

178
00:10:09.791 --> 00:10:11.875
This does not mean

179
00:10:11.875 --> 00:10:15.208
that you give up ambition.

180
00:10:15.208 --> 00:10:19.791
It means you give up the rush.

181
00:10:19.791 --> 00:10:24.458
Work hard, set high goals – but with peace

182
00:10:24.458 --> 00:10:27.000
and clarity, not with anxiety

183
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.500
and impatience.

184
00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.333
When you remain steady,

185
00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:35.208
your efforts start to connect and build.

186
00:10:35.208 --> 00:10:38.083
A true professional or worker

187
00:10:38.083 --> 00:10:41.833
moves forward not only with speed,
but with purpose

188
00:10:41.833 --> 00:10:45.000
and direction.

189
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.166
And when you work with contentment,

190
00:10:50.166 --> 00:10:53.375
you will find

191
00:10:53.375 --> 00:10:54.708
that I am

192
00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:58.208
quietly walking alongside you.
